14|// ⛔ THIS RUNNER USED TO PASS `config: false` AND `pool: 'threads'`, WHICH DISCARDED
15|// vitest.config.js ENTIRELY — the file `npm test` is supposed to be configured by.
16|//
17|// vitest.config.js pins two settings and explains at length why each is load-bearing:
18|// `pool: 'forks'` (relative-reporoot.test.js calls process.chdir(), which THROWS in the
19|// `threads` pool) and `fileParallelism: false` (real clangd/tsserver/pyright tests lose
20|// races for CPU when run concurrently). Both were written INTO THE CONFIG while this
21|// runner was already ignoring it, so `npm test` ran threads-parallel and failed 4 tests
22|// that pass under `node node_modules/vitest/vitest.mjs`. Same tree, two runners, two
23|// answers — and the documented command was the one that lied.
24|//
25|// ★ The config's own comment claims the requirement "travels with the repo rather than
26|// with my installed version". It did not travel as far as the repo's own test script.
27|// That is the recurring shape here: the fix reached one emitter, not the one people use.
28|//
29|// ⇒ Nothing about the suite is configured here now. include / timeouts / pool /
30|// fileParallelism have exactly one home. Guarded by tests/unit/test-runner-config.test.js.
31|const ctx = await startVitest(mode, filters, {
