2|//
3|// "Who calls X" is a set — order is a ranking question. "What does X call" is
4|// what an agent asks while reading a function body, and the useful order is the
5|// order the calls occur in.
6|//
7|// Field report (2026-07-27): graph_callees returned its list in an order that
8|// looked alphabetical/scrambled. Two causes stacked:
9|//   1. `rankCallees` was a literal alias of `rankCallers`, and for a callee list
10|//      EVERY tiebreaker in that function is constant (depth 1 at the default,
11|//      fan_in hardcoded to 1, from_type always 'Function'). All tiers collapsed
12|//      and the stable sort fell through to arbitrary SQL row order.
13|//   2. The mapper overwrote `source_line` with the CALLEE'S DEFINITION line,
14|//      discarding the only field that could express call order.
15|// The SQL also had no ORDER BY, so its LIMIT 100 truncated arbitrarily.
16|import { describe, it, expect, beforeEach, afterEach } from 'vitest';
17|import { mkdtemp, rm, mkdir } from 'node:fs/promises';
18|import { tmpdir } from 'node:os';
19|import { join } from 'node:path';
